{"name":"Anthracite","hex":"#28282d","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"anthracite","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A form of carbonized ancient plants; the hardest and cleanest-burning of all the coals.","A dark grey color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/anthracite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Anthracite","blocks":[{"text":"Anthracite, also known as hard coal and black coal, is a hard, compact variety of coal that has a submetallic lustre. It has the highest carbon content, the fewest impurities, and the highest energy density of all types of coal and is the highest ranking of coals."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Anthracite_chunk.JPG/330px-Anthracite_chunk.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anthracite","wikidata":"Q182458"},{"title":"Anthracite (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Anthracite is a six part French television series, created by Fanny Robert and Maxime Berthemy and released on 10 April 2024, on Netflix. Included in its cast are the rapper Hatik, Noémie Schmidt, and Camille Lou. It is loosely based on the Order of the Solar Temple, a group which was tied to several mass suicides. It is not a direct recreation of the Solar Temple story, as the group and people depicted are all wholly fictional."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/36/Anthracite_%28TV_series%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anthracite_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q125122358"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Coal_waste_pile_west_of_Trevorton%2C_Pennsylvania_far_shot_2.JPG/500px-Coal_waste_pile_west_of_Trevorton%2C_Pennsylvania_far_shot_2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Coal_waste_pile